; Stage 15 W8 (fn-pointer globals): the `null` gate in `defvar-init-ir` was
; widened to admit a bare function-pointer type — `(defvar h:(fn i32)(i32) null)`
; is legal, because a TY-FN slot carries no non-null contract and its implicit
; zero is already `null`.
;
; This is the boundary that widening must NOT cross. `ptr:(fn i32)(i32)` is a
; *pointer to* a function pointer, i.e. an ordinary PTR-REF typed pointer, so
; W6's `pkind-flow-check` still refuses `null` there. If this fixture ever
; compiles, the TY-FN admission has leaked past the kind it was written for and
; re-opened the hole W6 closed.

(defvar hp:ptr:(fn i32)(i32) null)

(defn main ():i32
  (return (unsafe/cast i32 (deref hp))))
